# Abort Landing sends DO_GO_AROUND with every parameter zero, and the vehicle answers it.
#
# BUT_abortland_Click is doAbortLand: doCommand(DO_GO_AROUND, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0). ArduCopter does
# not support it and says so; the answer in the message log is the proof it arrived.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1019-1032, ExtLibs/ArduPilot/Mavlink/MAVLinkInterface.cs:2660-2663`
#
# Needs SITL: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-abortland.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 2

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

click fly-abortland
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_DO_GO_AROUND 0,0,0,0,0,0,0
expect fly.ack ~ MAV_CMD_DO_GO_AROUND:
